+**Reel captions**: `caption: "Pick a style, hit *generate*"` (+ `captionAt:` its first local frame, or seconds like
+`0.5s`; default 4) on any reel block and on `media` — words pop one at a time (~3 a second, compressed so the last lands
+by ~72 % of the shot), white heavy type with an ink stroke, the newest word on an accent plate, at most 2 lines, at 70 %
+of the height on 9:16 (above the platform UI). A word runs from space to space, so `*generate*.` pops whole, accent and
+full stop together. Chinese and Japanese (no spaces between words) pop a character at a time: punctuation stays with its
+character, a Latin word or a number stays whole (`3.5`, `1,000`, `3:30`, `manus.im`), and straight quotes `"` open and
+close in turn (curly `“ ”` and `「 」` are never ambiguous). The storyboard/hero frame waits for the last word. At `--grid` a
+`captionAt` that is neither a frame nor seconds stops the run; a caption faster than ~5 words/s (CJK: characters/s), one
+whose last words would pop after the shot ends, and a `captionAt` past the shot's end warn.
 
+**Reel on/off fields** — sticker `shake` / `sparks` / `gloss` / `logo`, split `arrow`, float `streak`, cta `logo` — take
+`true` or `false`: YAML reads `no`, `off` and `"false"` as text, so `--grid` stops on them rather than leave the effect on.
+Sticker `tilt` is a number of degrees, −45…45 (`-5`, not `-5deg`).
